From 3ca1fba31d059f7c1b78a7e7ba07eb5eeb749157 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Steinhart <ssteinhart@student.tgm.ac.at>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:48:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add MO2947 (AX3295B, 2 MiB) board, flash-booted through
 the stock bootstrap

Board mo2947: the MOB/MO2947 promotional toy camera (Jinrixin/Buildwin AX3295B,
NV3030B 240x320 LCD, SP0A39 sensor, 4 MiB 5E4016 flash, 2 MiB SDRAM). Same pins
as the Action camera.

Boot: the image is linked at 0x02000000 and replaces the stock app in flash
(0x2200..); the unchanged stock header and bootstrap load it and call
0x020004A8. Sector 0 and the bootstrap are never modified. entry.S/early.c run
a minimal power hold and a SHUTTER-at-power-on escape to the boot ROM loader
before any SDK code, then jump to apx_spi_entry.

SDK changes (other boards unchanged):
- soc.h: memory map can come from a board's board_memory.h
- debug.c, display*.c, spi_overlay.c, runtime.c: use the memory-map macros
  instead of fixed 4 MiB addresses
- power.c: APX_PM40_HOLD (MO2947 stock holds PMU reg 0x40 = 0x0E)
- clock.c: APX_CLOCK_INHERIT; the AX3295B boot ROM leaves PLL1 at
  0x8858=0x1023/0x885C=0x112A8800 (144 MHz), not a JT5295 pair: keep it
- display_st7789.c: GPIO panel reset and backlight when the board has them
- camera.c: APX_SENSOR_LDO and APX_SENSOR_RESET_PD1 (stock MO2947 values)
- ffconf.h/storage.c: optional fixed FatFs code page (APX_FATFS_CODE_PAGE);
  the dynamic CJK tables (478 KB) do not fit the boot ROM's load window
- Makefile: BOARD=mo2947 builds a flat .bin; panel.inc is generated from the
  owner's flash dump and not committed

Examples: mo2947-demo (display/keys/LED/USB), mo2947-camera (camera preview,
SD, speaker, microphone, battery, USB debug link; all verified on the device).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
